From b6f7528f11bc77169612332e1f1e7f13736ef313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:55:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] hunt stress0: the patch scripts of the forcing hook and
 of the two scratch experiments

apply_hold_hook.py puts the forms publisher's hold into the src/db.rs of an
older tree (the forced schedule then runs there); apply_fix_b.py makes a
published form carry the log position it was settled at and a reader at an
older position build its own block; apply_fix_c.py makes the sameness test of
a rewritten partition compare every key. They take a path to a scratch copy of
the file, never the worktree's, and are experiments to price the two
mechanisms by removing them, not changes for the engine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
